---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Ken Lim — Full-Stack Data & AI" description="Ken Lim builds the whole path from raw data to production AI: pipelines, curated and governed data, ML models, and AI agents. Hands-on data tech lead, 18+ years across fintech, healthtech, proptech and the public sector.">

  <!-- letterhead / hero -->
  <section class="relative pt-16 pb-10 sm:pt-24">
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">
      Full-Stack Data &amp; AI<span class="text-stone-300">.</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-mono text-[12.5px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">New York City · 18+ years experience · U.S. citizen</p>
    <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap justify-start gap-x-6 gap-y-2 font-mono text-[12px]">
      <a class="text-[#03aa5c] hover:underline dark:text-[#3cc287]" href="mailto:mail@kennylim.com">mail@kennylim.com</a>
      <a class="text-stone-500 hover:text-[#03aa5c] dark:text-stone-400 dark:hover:text-stone-100" href="tel:+19298889061">+1 (929) 888-9061</a>
      <a class="text-stone-500 hover:text-[#03aa5c] dark:text-stone-400 dark:hover:text-stone-100" href="https://linkedin.com/in/kenny-lim" rel="noopener" target="_blank">LinkedIn ↗</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 1. about me -->
  <section data-reveal class="border-t border-stone-200/80 py-12 dark:border-stone-800">
    <p class="font-displaymono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.35em] text-stone-400">01 — who I am</p>
    <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">About me</h2>
    <div class="mt-5 space-y-4 text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300">
      <p>
        My approach is simple: understand the real needs of stakeholders, map the gap between
        where the data is and where it should be, then architect and build what closes it,
        from pipelines, curated and governed data, and BI to ML models and RAG and agent
        services in production. Along the way, I build and lead the data teams that keep it
        running.
      </p>
      <p>
        I've never stopped doing the elbow-grease work, and I eat my own dog food: I write the
        code, ship it, and run it. Having owned every layer, I know what a design really costs
        to build and maintain. That means fewer handoffs, faster delivery, and systems that
        last.
      </p>
      <p>
        Consulting taught me to work this way. After earning my M.S. in Software Engineering
        from Carnegie Mellon, I spent a decade delivering big-data platforms for clients
        ranging from startups to Fortune 500 companies and the U.S. Department of Defense,
        where every engagement had to deliver real results on a real budget. Since then, I've
        built data and AI platforms in-house at companies like N26 across fintech, healthtech,
        SaaS, and proptech, and was part of three successful exits. Today I'm at the
        International Atomic Energy Agency, where I help architect and build an air-gapped
        lakehouse and its data pipelines, audited and validated by PwC. I'm also pursuing a
        thesis-track M.S. in Artificial Intelligence at UT Austin.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-8 font-mono text-[12px] text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">
      Where I've done it → <a class="text-[#03aa5c] hover:underline dark:text-[#3cc287]" href={base + "/experience"}>Experience</a>
    </p>
  </section>

</Layout>
